concepts.statement:
A **function definition expression** defines a function value — usually anonymous — with the `function` keyword:
```js
const square = function (x) { return x * x; };    // anonymous
const f = function fact(n) {                      // NAMED expression
  return n <= 1 ? 1 : n * fact(n - 1);           // name enables recursion
};
const sq = (x) => x * x;                           // arrow (ES6)
```
When a name is present it becomes a binding **inside the function only** — invisible outside, perfect for recursion. Arrows are more than shorthand: they also inherit `this` instead of receiving one (Chapter 8).

