```
let s = JSON.stringify(lecture);
// '{"title":"Closures","room":null,"when":"2027-03-14T00:00:00.000Z"}'
```

```
class SerializableSet extends Set {
  toJSON() {
    return [...this]; // spread the members into an array — Chapter 7
  }
}
```

concepts.detail:
```
let calculator = {
  value: 0,
  add(n) { this.value += n; return this; },
};
calculator.add(2).add(3); // .value is 5 — returning this chains calls
```
Returning `this` from mutating methods is the **method chaining** idiom behind fluent APIs.

```
const point = {
  x: 3, y: 4,
  toString() { return `(${this.x}, ${this.y})`; },
  valueOf() { return Math.hypot(this.x, this.y); }
};
String(point)  // "(3, 4)" — toString
point * 2      // 10 — valueOf gives 5, then doubled
```
There is also a locale-aware `toLocaleString()` hook used by internationalized code (Chapter 11).

```
function makePoint(x, y) {
  return { x, y }; // same as { x: x, y: y }
}
makePoint(1, 2) // { x: 1, y: 2 }
```

```
let prop = "main";
let config = { [prop]: 1, [`${prop}Title"]: "Config" };
// { main: 1, mainTitle: "Config" }
```
The expression may evaluate to a string or a **symbol** — computed keys are the only way to use a symbol key in a literal.

```
const SIZE = Symbol("size");
const stack = {
  [SIZE]: 0,
  push(v) { this[SIZE]++; return v; }
};
Object.keys(stack) // ["push"] — SIZE is hidden
```
Hidden is not private (anyone holding the symbol can read it), but accidental access and name collisions are both out of the picture.

```
let circle = {
  r: 1,
  area() { return Math.PI * this.r ** 2; },
  *[Symbol.iterator]() { yield this.r; } // generator shorthand, Chapter 12
};
circle.area() // 3.141592653589793
```

```
const user = {
  _name: "",
  get name() { return this._name; },
  set name(v) {
    if (typeof v !== "string" || v.length === 0) throw new TypeError("bad name");
    this._name = v;
  }
};
```
The leading underscore marks the backing data property as internal by convention only — real privacy needs closures (Section 8.5) or `#` private fields (Chapter 9).

steps.text:
