```
let source = [1, 2, 3];
let a2 = [...source];
```
Best for copying or combining: `a2` shares no identity with `source` — push to one and the other is unchanged (though nested objects are shared).

```
let b = ["a", "b", "c", "d"];
b.splice(1, 1);
