concepts.detail:
```
const square = x => x * x;
const add = (x, y) => x + y;
const noop = () => {};
```
When `this` binding matters — method definitions on objects, constructors — arrows are usually the wrong tool (Sections 8.2 and 9.3); when you need `this` *inherited* — callbacks inside methods — they are the fix (the worked example in 8.2).

