chart.whereAmI();
```
→ the `chart` object itself: the property-access-then-call form made `chart` the receiver. `whereAmI` was not written for charts — the call form did the binding.

```
"use strict";
const timer = {
  started: false,
  start() { this.started = true; }
};
setTimeout(timer.start, 10); // later: TypeError
```
`timer.start` is evaluated first — producing the function **detached from `timer`** — and that function is what setTimeout receives.

```
