concepts.statement:
Flanagan’s canonical iterable — a numeric range inclusive of both ends:
```js
class Range {
  constructor(from, to) {
    this.from = from;
    this.to = to;
  }

  [Symbol.iterator]() {
    let next = this.from;         // cursor state, local to THIS iteration
    const last = this.to;
    return {
      next() {
        return next <= last
          ? { value: next++, done: false }
          : { value: undefined, done: true };
      }
    };
  }
}
```
Every loop over a Range gets a brand-new cursor starting at `from`.

