``` The `raw` array is why a tag can tell the difference between a tab and the two characters backslash-t.

```js
const seen = new WeakMap();
function sql(strings, ...values) {
  if (!seen.has(strings)) seen.set(strings, strings.join('?'));
  return { text: seen.get(strings), values };   // parse once, run many times
}
```
Caching is why tags can afford to parse the literal (a mini-language compile) on first use and skip it afterwards — the array identity is the call-site key.

```js
