concepts.detail:
```js
describe("formatPrice", () => {
  it("rounds to two decimals", () => { /* ... */ });
  it("prefixes the currency", () => { /* ... */ });
});
```
Good suite names are sentences: `it("returns empty for an empty cart")`. The failure output then reads like a broken spec — which is the entire debugging clue.

```js
describe("cart", () => {
  let cart;
  beforeEach(() => {
    cart = createCart();       // every it() starts from zero
  });
  it("adds items", () => { cart.add("apple"); ... });
  it("starts empty", () => { expect(cart.size()).toBe(0); });
});
```
Without the hook, `starts empty` depends on running before `adds items` — the suite becomes order-sensitive and intermittently red, the worst state a test suite can be in.

```js
