  await expect(Promise.resolve(42)).resolves.toBe(42);
});
test("rejects", async () => {
  await expect(Promise.reject(new Error("x"))).rejects.toThrow("x");
});
```
The classic rookie bug: forgetting the `return`/`await` — the test finishes before the promise settles and passes vacuously. Always awaiting is the discipline that closes that hole (Section 13.3 habits, reused).

