Parameter destructuring documents the expected shape while `textContent` renders safely with no HTML parsing involved.

```js
const adminCount = members.reduce((n, m) => n + (m.role === "admin" ? 1 : 0), 0);
const firstAda = members.find((m) => m.name === "Ada");
```
Reduce folds the roster into one tally and find locates a single record, completing the read toolkit alongside the pipeline.

```js
const defaults = { theme: "light", pageSize: 20, filters: ["new"] };
const overrides = { theme: "dark" };
const settings = { ...defaults, ...overrides, filters: [...defaults.filters, "sale"] };
```
Later spreads win per key while the nested array merges explicitly, leaving both inputs untouched for reuse.

```js
// settings.js
export const settings = { theme: "dark", pageSize: 20 };
export function pageSize() { return settings.pageSize; }
export default settings;
```
Named exports share pieces while the default carries the whole record, giving importers precise or wholesale access.

```js
// app.js
import settings, { pageSize } from "./settings.js";
console.log("page size:", pageSize());
```
Static imports declare the dependency graph in code, enabling bundlers to tree-shake unused exports automatically.

```js
// DANGEROUS: never do this with untrusted data
list.innerHTML += "<li><b>" + comment.author + "</b>: " + comment.body + "</li>";
```
String concatenation into `innerHTML` parses attacker markup, so a body containing an image with an error handler would execute script.

```js
function commentNode({ author, body, official }) {
  const li = document.createElement("li");
  const who = document.createElement("b");
  who.textContent = author;
  li.append(who, ": " + body);
  if (official) { li.classList.add("official"); }
  return li;
}
```
Every untrusted string lands in `textContent` or string append context that serializes as text, while trust (official flag) travels as a boolean, not markup.

```css
.official::after { content: " ✓"; color: #16a34a; font-weight: 700; }
```
```js
const frag = document.createDocumentFragment();
comments.map(commentNode).forEach((li) => frag.append(li));
list.append(frag);
```
The badge draws from CSS generated content — no markup needed — and the fragment inserts the whole feed in one reflow.

```js
const tabs = document.querySelector(".tabs");
tabs.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
  const tab = event.target.closest('[role="tab"]');
  if (!tab) { return; }
  tabs.querySelectorAll('[role="tab"]').forEach((t) => {
    t.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(t === tab));
    t.classList.toggle("active", t === tab);
  });
  tabs.querySelectorAll('[role="tabpanel"]').forEach((p) => {
    p.hidden = p.id !== tab.dataset.panel;
  });
});
```
One listener resolves the clicked tab with `closest()`, then syncs classes, ARIA selection and panel visibility in a single pass.

