steps.text:
Encode filters rather than concatenating strings by hand:
```js
const url = new URL("https://api.example.com/articles");
url.searchParams.set("limit", "10");
url.searchParams.set("cursor", "abc123");
```

Branch on status before touching the body:
```js
const res = await fetch(url, {
  headers: { Accept: "application/json" }
});
if (!res.ok) {
  throw new Error("List failed with status " + res.status);
}
const page = await res.json();
```

Confirm the shape the docs promised:
```js
if (!Array.isArray(page.data)) {
  throw new Error("Unexpected list shape");
}
renderList(page.data);
```

Create one controller per submission:
```js
const ctrl = new AbortController();
const timer = setTimeout(function () { ctrl.abort(); }, 5000);
```

Stringify the payload and label its content type:
```js
let res;
try {
  res = await fetch("https://api.example.com/comments", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify({ postId: 9, text: "Great post" }),
    signal: ctrl.signal
  });
} finally {
  clearTimeout(timer);
}
```

Handle aborts, HTTP errors, and success on separate paths:
```js
if (!res.ok) {
  throw new Error("Create failed with status " + res.status);
}
const created = await res.json();
appendComment(created);
```

Surround the call with handling that names aborts:
```js
try {
  await postComment();
} catch (err) {
  showNotice(err.name === "AbortError" ? "Timed out, try again" : err.message);
}
```

