Take control of the unit boundary before touching balances:
```java
try (Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:derby:studyDB")) {
    // all-or-nothing-pattern: disable auto commit, settle explicitly
    conn.setAutoCommit(false);
    try (Statement stat = conn.createStatement()) {
        stat.executeUpdate("UPDATE Accounts SET Balance = Balance - 100 WHERE Id = 1");
        stat.executeUpdate("UPDATE Accounts SET Balance = Balance + 100 WHERE Id = 2");
        conn.commit();
        System.out.println("transferred");
    } catch (SQLException e) {
        try {
            conn.rollback();
        } catch (SQLException r) {
            System.err.println("rollback failed: " + r.getMessage());
        }
        System.err.println("rolled back: " + e.getMessage());
    } finally {
        conn.setAutoCommit(true);
    }
} catch (SQLException e) {
    System.err.println("transfer failed: " + e.getMessage());
}
```
Both statements share one private workspace.

Fill one prepared insert with two parameter sets:
```java
try (Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:derby:studyDB");
     PreparedStatement stat = conn.prepareStatement(
         "INSERT INTO Books (Author, Title) VALUES (?, ?)")) {
    // batch-insert-pattern: queue rows client side, send in one round trip
    conn.setAutoCommit(false);
    Savepoint mark = conn.setSavepoint();
    String[][] rows = {{"Tolkien", "The Hobbit"}, {"Le Guin", "Earthsea"}};
    for (String[] row : rows) {
        stat.setString(1, row[0]);
        stat.setString(2, row[1]);
        stat.addBatch();
    }
    stat.executeBatch();
    conn.releaseSavepoint(mark);
    conn.commit();
    System.out.println("batch committed");
} catch (SQLException e) {
    System.err.println("batch failed: " + e.getMessage());
}
```
One network trip carries both rows.

