concepts.statement:
Each **strong entity** set becomes a table with its attributes as columns and its primary key as **`PRIMARY KEY`**: `Employee(EmpId, Name, Salary)` maps to ```sql
CREATE TABLE Employee(EmpId INT PRIMARY KEY, Name TEXT, Salary INT);
``` Composite attributes flatten; derived attributes are omitted.

steps.text:
Map the strong sets. ```sql
CREATE TABLE Department(DeptNo INT PRIMARY KEY, DName TEXT);
CREATE TABLE Employee(EmpId INT PRIMARY KEY, Name TEXT,
  DeptNo INT NOT NULL REFERENCES Department(DeptNo));
```
The $1:N$ link adds no table; total participation makes `DeptNo NOT NULL`.

Map the two entity sets. ```sql
CREATE TABLE Student(RollNo INT PRIMARY KEY, Name TEXT);
CREATE TABLE Course(CourseId INT PRIMARY KEY, Title TEXT);
```

concepts.statement:
**Entity integrity**: no part of any **primary key** may be **`NULL`**, enforced automatically by every `PRIMARY KEY` declaration. A null key would create an unidentifiable tuple, so ```sql
CREATE TABLE T(A INT PRIMARY KEY, B INT);
``` rejects any insert with `A` null.

steps.text:
Universal form. ```text
{ s.RollNo | Student(s) ∧ (∀c)(Core(c) → Takes(s.RollNo, c)) }
```

concepts.statement:
The **`WHERE`** clause keeps individual tuples satisfying a boolean predicate, for example ```sql
SELECT Name FROM Employee WHERE DeptNo = 10 AND Salary > 50000;
``` Only rows evaluating to **`TRUE`** survive; `FALSE` and `UNKNOWN` (null comparisons) are discarded identically.

Every bare (non-aggregated) column in `SELECT` or `HAVING` must appear in **`GROUP BY`** (or be functionally determined by it): ```sql
SELECT DeptNo, AVG(Salary) FROM Employee GROUP BY DeptNo;
``` Grouping by `DeptNo` yields one row per department; selecting an ungrouped `Name` beside it is rejected because one group holds many names.

**`ALTER TABLE`** evolves structure (`ADD COLUMN`, `DROP COLUMN`, `ADD CONSTRAINT`); **`DROP TABLE`** removes structure **and** data; **`DELETE`** removes **rows only**, keeping the schema. ```sql
ALTER TABLE Employee ADD COLUMN Email TEXT UNIQUE;
``` migrates live tables, while `DROP TABLE EmpPhone` erases the table itself.

